key_findings:
Raw K5 critical path (mean 2063 ms):
- q34: 1011 ms (49 %) = device 431 + front 268 + untimed host glue 169 + host inside the calls 135 + tail 8;
- tower: 671 ms (33 %), of which the window static(5) + phase-A staircase is 415;
- census: 218 ms (10.6 %);
- merge, indexes, prepare and residual: about 163 ms.

q2 is fully hidden: q2_wait = 0 in all 12 GPU cases.

The GPU helps least on raw frames:
- engine/GPU chain speedup is 2.47–2.69 at raw K5 vs 2.64–2.92 without ground, and 2.18–2.31 at raw K10 vs 2.51–2.74;
- q34 speedup at K10 is 3.98–4.25 at raw vs 4.63–5.02;
- the device is busy only 20–22 % of the raw chain (kernels 16–19 %);
- the 48-thread CPU sits idle for 366–433 ms during the device calls even after q2;
- lanes transfers reach 266–292 ms at raw K10, 35–43 % of the lanes device time.
